-- Typechecks cleanly. An export with no inputs answers a list inside its own
-- JUST, and the list ends in a refusal one level below the depth a directive
-- reads, because the rule's JUST takes a level. `l4 run` answers it, and
-- `l4 batch` must too: with no inputs it asks for the export bare, so there
-- is no JUST of its own to see through.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`refusal in the list` n MEANS
  IF n EQUALS 0 THEN LIST (REFUSE "deep") ELSE n FOLLOWED BY `refusal in the list` (n MINUS 1)

@export a list in the rule's own JUST, ending in a refusal below the depth read
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF NUMBER)
`wrapped` MEANS JUST (`refusal in the list` 200)

#EVAL `wrapped`
